<title>NETHERLANDS: Fortis, NIB put venture cap study on hold.</title>
<headline>Fortis, NIB put venture cap study on hold.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Nationale Investeringsbank NIB said on Friday that studies into the possibility of a venture capital joint venture with Dutch-Belgian financial group Fortis had been put on hold.  </p>
<p>&quot;The reason is the recently announced takeover of MeesPierson NV by Fortis Nederland,&quot; NIB said in a statement. It said the venture capital units involved were NIB's PARNIB Holding and Fortis' NeSBIC Group NV.</p>
<p>Fortis and NIB said last April they were investigating the possibilities of merging their venture capital activities to bolster their position in the risk-bearing capital market.</p>
<p>Fortis signed a letter of intent to take over ABN Amro's merchant bank MeesPierson last October, rounding off the acquisition in December, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
